INT. AIR DUCT - ABOVE VAULT CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Cramped aluminum. A pencil flashlight in his teeth. Dust motes. The distant hum of a security camera swiveling below.

ANDREJ MOKOENA, 30s, crawls on his elbows with a coil of rope on his back and a small recorder strapped to his sleeve. He stops at a vent grate. Looks down at a laser grid.

He spits the flashlight into his hand. Whispers.

ANDREJ
Okay. Okay. Rehearsal one.

He taps the recorder. Plays it.

ANDREJ (V.O.)
(recorded, whisper)
Step one. Rope on the vent bolt. Step two. Lower down, slow, between beam three and beam four. Step three. Don't sneeze.

He winces.

ANDREJ
I'm going to sneeze.

He pinches his nose. Waits. It passes. He taps the recorder again.

ANDREJ (V.O.)
(recorded)
Step four. The safe's a Hargrove. Combination is the date of the Armistice, flipped. Eleven eleven, nineteen eighteen, so one-one, one-one, one-eight, one-nine.

ANDREJ
That's seven numbers. Hargrove's six.

He frowns. Rewinds.

ANDREJ (V.O.)
(recorded)
...one-one, one-one, one-eight, one-nine...

ANDREJ
Drop the last nine. One-one, one-one, one-eight.

He whispers it three times, like a spell, then taps the recorder to start a new take.

ANDREJ (CONT'D)
Rehearsal two. If I die in this duct, tell my mother I was a pastry chef.

A click below. A faint red light sweeps across the vent. He freezes. The light passes.

ANDREJ (CONT'D)
(barely audible)
Step one.

He slides the first bolt loose.
